<p id="p2">It happens to all of us. You come across an article you want to read, but you’re in the middle of something and don’t have the time. <a href="https://goodlinks.app/" rel="noopener noreferrer">GoodLinks</a> gives those articles a home on your iPhone, iPad, and Mac, with a clean, customizable reading experience when you’re ready to return to them.</p>
<p id="p3">Recently updated for iOS, iPadOS, and macOS 27, GoodLinks lets you organize the articles you save for later with tags and stars before sitting down to read with its highly customizable reader. Article Sync, which is part of GoodLinks Premium, can sync complete articles along with their images through iCloud, so they’re available on every device.</p>
<p id="p4">GoodLinks also lets you highlight your favorite passages of articles, export your highlights as Markdown, and add notes to your highlights. Plus, GoodLinks has extensive Shortcuts support, allowing you to use what you save with your other apps and workflows, and a local API on the Mac to script your links, tags, and highlights.</p>
<p id="p5">The app can summarize articles using Apple Intelligence on compatible devices or external AI providers when you provide your own API keys. That allows you to use the model that suits your needs best, or you can turn off summarization entirely.</p>
<p id="p6">A single universal purchase covers iPhone, iPad, and Mac and includes all current features plus one year of feature upgrades. Everything you unlock is yours to keep. After that, an optional GoodLinks Premium subscription unlocks new features, which you keep even if you cancel.</p>
<p id="p7">Whether you’re catching up on your latest saved stories or building a complex reading workflow to handle hundreds of articles, <a href="https://goodlinks.app/" rel="noopener noreferrer">visit GoodLinks to learn more and download the app today</a>.</p>
